{"id":"perizzites","name":"Perizzites","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:perizzites"],"types":[{"type":"group","from":"UBS: Names of Groups"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Perizzites","text":"Villagers; dwellers in the open country, the Canaanitish nation inhabiting the fertile regions south and south-west of Carmel. “They were the graziers, farmers, and peasants of the time.” They were to be driven out of the land by the descendants of Abraham (Gen. 15:20; Ex. 3:8, 17; 23:23; 33:2; 34:11). They are afterwards named among the conquered tribes (Josh. 24:11). Still lingering in the land, however, they were reduced to servitude by Solomon (1 Kings 9:20)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6522","lemma":"פְּרִזִּי","xlit":"Pᵉrizzîy","gloss":"a Perizzite, one of the Canaanitish tribes","kjv":"Perizzite","count":7,"share":0.7},{"strong":"H776","lemma":"אֶרֶץ","xlit":"ʼerets","gloss":"the earth","kjv":"common, country, earth, field","count":4,"share":0.4},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":4,"share":0.4}],"verses":["Gen.13.7","Gen.15.20","Exod.3.8","Exod.23.23","Deut.20.17","Judg.3.5","Ezra.9.1","Judg.3.6","Judg.3.7","Ezra.9.2"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"canaanites","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"jebusites","type":"cooccur","shared":7,"jaccard":0.127,"why":"7 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"hittites","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.118,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"hivites","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.118,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"miscegenation","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.103,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"amorites","type":"cooccur","shared":7,"jaccard":0.038